{"blocks":[["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-5091","DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand is a startup hook -> False. It is tied to client attachment, not just container process startup.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-5240","DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand is part of every local workflow -> False. It is more relevant in prebuild-oriented workflows than in typical local VS Code usage.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-5425","DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand can rely on container tools -> False. It runs on the host, before the container exists.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-5565","Quick Reference",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-6335","Related",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-6349","DevContainer",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-6370","DevContainer/Ref/Key",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-6399","DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-51","initializeCommand",[]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-73","Overview",["initializeCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-88","initializeCommand is the earliest standard DevContainer lifecycle hook.",["initializeCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-166","It runs on the host machine before the container is created or built.",["initializeCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-240","When It Is Called",["initializeCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-264","During creation or rebuild flows, before Docker has finished building or starting the dev container.",["initializeCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-369","Because it runs before the container exists, it cannot rely on tools that only live inside the container image.",["initializeCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-485","Why You Would Use It",["initializeCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-512","Use it when the environment needs host-side preparation before container creation can proceed.",["initializeCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-611","Typical cases include:",["initializeCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-638","Checking whether required local tools or files exist",["initializeCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-696","Generating files that the Docker build or devcontainer.json depends on",["initializeCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-774","Preparing host-side credentials or configuration inputs",["initializeCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-835","Mutating .devcontainer inputs before the build starts",["initializeCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-896","Mental Model",["initializeCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-915","Treat initializeCommand as the \"prepare the inputs\" hook.",["initializeCommand","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-979","If the work must happen before the container build and startup sequence, this is the right place.",["initializeCommand","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-1081","Misconceptions",["initializeCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-1102","It runs inside the container -> False. It runs on the host.",["initializeCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-1174","It is a good place for package installation in the dev container -> False. Container package installation belongs in the image build or a container-side hook.",["initializeCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-1345","Related",["initializeCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand/","source-block-1359","DevContainer/Hook",["initializeCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-51","onCreateCommand",[]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-71","Overview",["onCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-86","onCreateCommand is a first-creation hook that runs inside the container after the container has been created and started.",["onCreateCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-214","It runs once per container creation, not on every restart.",["onCreateCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-277","When It Is Called",["onCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-301","After the initial build and container startup for a new dev container instance.",["onCreateCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-385","It does not rerun just because the container starts again later.",["onCreateCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-454","Why You Would Use It",["onCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-481","Use it for one-time bootstrap steps that should happen when the environment first comes into existence.",["onCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-589","Typical cases include:",["onCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-616","Initial project bootstrapping",["onCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-651","One-time tool or dependency setup",["onCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-690","Safe-directory Git configuration",["onCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-728","Migrations or initialization tasks that should not repeat on every start",["onCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-806","Practical Distinction",["onCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-834","onCreateCommand is about first creation.",["onCreateCommand","Practical Distinction"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-883","If the task should instead run after the workspace is fully mounted and ready for normal project setup, [[DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand]] is often a better fit.",["onCreateCommand","Practical Distinction"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-1056","Misconceptions",["onCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-1077","It runs on every restart -> False. It only runs when the container is first created.",["onCreateCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-1174","It replaces postCreateCommand for all setup -> False. Many teams still prefer postCreateCommand for the main dependency-install step.",["onCreateCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-1324","Related",["onCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-1338","DevContainer/Hook",["onCreateCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand/","source-block-1364","DevContainer/Ref/Key",["onCreateCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-51","postAttachCommand",[]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-73","Overview",["postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-88","postAttachCommand runs inside the container whenever a tool session attaches to it.",["postAttachCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-178","It is the most user-session-oriented hook in the standard lifecycle set.",["postAttachCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-255","When It Is Called",["postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-279","After the initial attach to a newly created or started dev container.",["postAttachCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-353","Again on later reattach events, such as window reloads or reconnects.",["postAttachCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-427","Why You Would Use It",["postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-454","Use it for tasks that only make sense when a developer-facing client has attached.",["postAttachCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-541","Typical cases include:",["postAttachCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-568","Session-oriented UX initialization",["postAttachCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-608","Printing banners or usage hints",["postAttachCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-645","Starting interactive processes tied to the attached session",["postAttachCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-710","Running commands that are useful on each editor attach",["postAttachCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-770","Practical Distinction",["postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-798","postAttachCommand is about the developer session becoming active.",["postAttachCommand","Practical Distinction"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-870","If the task should happen even without a client attach, [[DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand]] is the better hook.",["postAttachCommand","Practical Distinction"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-991","Misconceptions",["postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-1012","It is just another startup hook -> False. It is tied to attach events, not only container startup.",["postAttachCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-1123","It only runs once -> False. It can run again on reattach or window reload.",["postAttachCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-1210","Related",["postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-1224","DevContainer/Hook",["postAttachCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand/","source-block-1250","DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand",["postAttachCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-51","postCreateCommand",[]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-73","Overview",["postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-88","postCreateCommand runs inside the container after the environment has been created and the workspace is mounted.",["postCreateCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-207","In practice, this is the hook many teams use for their main project setup step.",["postCreateCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-291","When It Is Called",["postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-315","After first creation, once the workspace is ready inside the container.",["postCreateCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-391","It does not rerun on ordinary container restarts.",["postCreateCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-445","Why You Would Use It",["postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-472","Use it for project-level setup that depends on the actual checked-out workspace being present.",["postCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-571","Typical cases include:",["postCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-598","Running npm install, pnpm install, pip install, or similar dependency installation",["postCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-692","Finalizing project configuration",["postCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-730","Running setup scripts that need the workspace mount",["postCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-787","Preparing local development tooling after the container exists",["postCreateCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-855","Practical Distinction",["postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-883","postCreateCommand is usually the best fit when the setup depends on repository files being mounted and available.",["postCreateCommand","Practical Distinction"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-1003","That is why it is often preferred over [[DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand]] for the main dependency-install step.",["postCreateCommand","Practical Distinction"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-1124","Misconceptions",["postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-1145","It runs every time the container starts -> False. It is a creation-time hook, not a restart hook.",["postCreateCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-1255","It should replace image builds for everything -> False. Stable base tooling often belongs in the image, not in a post-create step.",["postCreateCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-1398","Related",["postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand/","source-block-1412","DevContainer/Hook",["postCreateCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-51","postStartCommand",[]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-72","Overview",["postStartCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-87","postStartCommand runs inside the container every time the container starts.",["postStartCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-169","It is the runtime hook for re-establishing state that should exist whenever the container becomes live.",["postStartCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-277","When It Is Called",["postStartCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-301","On the initial container start after creation.",["postStartCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-352","On every later restart of that container.",["postStartCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-398","Why You Would Use It",["postStartCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-425","Use it for repeatable runtime tasks that should happen each time the environment starts.",["postStartCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-518","Typical cases include:",["postStartCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-545","Starting background services",["postStartCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-579","Recreating temporary runtime state",["postStartCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-619","Running idempotent initialization checks",["postStartCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-665","Preparing the live environment for normal use",["postStartCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-716","Mental Model",["postStartCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-735","Treat postStartCommand as the \"container is live again\" hook.",["postStartCommand","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-803","Because it runs repeatedly, commands here should be safe to rerun.",["postStartCommand","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-874","Misconceptions",["postStartCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-895","It is only for the first creation -> False. It also runs on subsequent restarts.",["postStartCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-988","It is the same as postAttachCommand -> False. Startup and client attachment are different events.",["postStartCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-1100","Related",["postStartCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-1114","DevContainer/Hook",["postStartCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand/","source-block-1140","DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand",["postStartCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-51","updateContentCommand",[]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-76","Overview",["updateContentCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-91","updateContentCommand is a container-side hook for cases where workspace content changes during the creation flow.",["updateContentCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-211","It exists to reconcile environment setup with repository content that may not have been finalized at the earlier build stage.",["updateContentCommand","Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-341","When It Is Called",["updateContentCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-365","During creation workflows where content updates happen after the image build step, such as GitHub Codespaces prebuild-oriented flows.",["updateContentCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-503","It is not commonly the main hook in typical local VS Code usage.",["updateContentCommand","When It Is Called"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-572","Why You Would Use It",["updateContentCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-599","Use it when your environment setup depends on repository contents that may arrive or change after the image has already been prepared.",["updateContentCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-738","Typical cases include:",["updateContentCommand","Why You Would Use It"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-765","Refreshing generated artifacts after content sync",["updateContentCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-820","Re-running workspace-dependent setup in prebuild scenarios",["updateContentCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-884","Reconciling dependency state with post-build content changes",["updateContentCommand","Why You Would Use It","Typical cases include:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-950","Mental Model",["updateContentCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-969","Treat updateContentCommand as the \"content changed during creation\" hook.",["updateContentCommand","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-1049","It is mainly about staged creation pipelines rather than ordinary local restarts.",["updateContentCommand","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-1135","Misconceptions",["updateContentCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-1156","It runs during every local create in a visible way -> False. Many local workflows barely surface it.",["updateContentCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-1269","It is the same as postCreateCommand -> False. It addresses a narrower content-change case during creation.",["updateContentCommand","Misconceptions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-1390","Related",["updateContentCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand/","source-block-1404","DevContainer/Hook",["updateContentCommand","Related"]],["DevContainer/How%20To/Get%20Github%20Command%20Line%20Inside%20Dev%20Container/","source-block-0","GitHub CLI on devcontainer - DEV Community - how to get GitHub/CLI in a DevContainer",[]],["DevContainer/How%20To/Get%20Github%20Command%20Line%20Inside%20Dev%20Container/","source-block-154","To use the GitHub CLI (a.k.a. gh) on devcontainer, you need to pass credentials for that.",["GitHub CLI on devcontainer - DEV Community - how to get GitHub/CLI in a DevContainer"]],["DevContainer/How%20To/Open%20both%20Dev%20Container%20and%20non-Dev%20Container%20at%20same%20time/","source-block-0","Q - what's the easiest way to be able to run commands in the repo without DevContainer open while having the dev container open?",[]],["DevContainer/How%20To/Open%20both%20Dev%20Container%20and%20non-Dev%20Container%20at%20same%20time/","source-block-141","useful for accessing things that haven't been added yet to the container, for example, , or opening files in the host operating system",["Q - what's the easiest way to be able to run commands in the repo without DevContainer open while having the dev container open?"]],["DevContainer/Idea/Agentic%20System%20to%20Setup%20DevContainer/","source-block-44","Using Agentic AI systems to generate Dev Containers",[]],["DevContainer/Idea/Agentic%20System%20to%20Setup%20DevContainer/","source-block-100","https://devcontainer.ai/ is an example, but it's not opensource",["Using Agentic AI systems to generate Dev Containers"]],["DevContainer/lock.json/","source-block-0","via https://github.com/devcontainers/cli/tree/main/.devcontainer",[]],["DevContainer/lock.json/","source-block-67","there's now a devcontainer-lock.json which locks the osi image ... not sure what produces this",["via https://github.com/devcontainers/cli/tree/main/.devcontainer"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-0","Do I need an IDE to use a DevContainer in practice?",[]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-60","For example, could I make it so that from my terminal, I launch my devcontainer, and then I'm now using the terminal inside my devcontainer?",["Do I need an IDE to use a DevContainer in practice?"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-204","Answer",[]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-216","Short answer: no, you do not need an IDE to use a devcontainer.",["Answer"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-287","A devcontainer is just Docker + conventions + metadata. IDEs like VS Code or JetBrains are merely clients that automate the lifecycle.",["Answer"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-431","You can absolutely launch and live inside it from a plain terminal.",["Answer"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-502","Mental model",["Answer"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-522","A devcontainer is basically:",["Answer","Mental model"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-555","Dockerfile or image",["Answer","Mental model","A devcontainer is basically:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-584","optional docker-compose.yml",["Answer","Mental model","A devcontainer is basically:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-619",".devcontainer/devcontainer.json (metadata + setup hooks)",["Answer","Mental model","A devcontainer is basically:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-683","IDE features = convenience only:",["Answer","Mental model"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-720","build",["Answer","Mental model","IDE features = convenience only:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-731","start",["Answer","Mental model","IDE features = convenience only:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-742","exec into container",["Answer","Mental model","IDE features = convenience only:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-767","mount source",["Answer","Mental model","IDE features = convenience only:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-785","forward ports",["Answer","Mental model","IDE features = convenience only:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-804","run postCreate/postStart commands",["Answer","Mental model","IDE features = convenience only:"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-843","All of that can be done manually or via CLI.",["Answer","Mental model"]],["DevContainer/Q/Do%20I%20need%20an%20IDE%20to%20use%20a%20devcontainer%20in%20practice/","source-block-892","Option 1 — Pure Docker (simplest, zero tooling)",["Answer"]]],"format_version":5}